  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat has a whitelisting system for video player and livestream hosts, shown here: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/www-whitelist\nbut the whitelist itself has not been updated for some time.\nUnfortunately one of the most widely used VRChat streaming services is still not on the whitelist: TopazChat ( `*.topaz.chat` )\nSee here for the absurdly complex instructions that the JP community is forced to do.\nhttps://twitter.com/Coquelicots_WoT/status/1581208227382906880\nWhen users do this, they are opening themselves up for all worlds, due to the fact that whitelists were rushed in 2 years ago and never updated.\nFurthermore, *official events* and unofficial events often ask participants to enable Allow Untrusted URLs. VRChat should work with event planners to resolve this in the whitelist so once again you don't have users opening themselves up to privacy leaks.\nRegards,\nLyuma",
